{"id":"254177605ed47637","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-df-reflection.md","title":"Finite-Fragment Reflection","display":"df-reflection — Finite-Fragment Reflection","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-reflection","aliases":["58-df-reflection"],"display":"df-reflection — Finite-Fragment Reflection","depends_on":["[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-substructure.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-finite.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-reflection"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-reflection</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-reflection — Finite-Fragment Reflection"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"563f382027630287\" href=\"?note=563f382027630287\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-substructure.md\">../batch13/58-df-substructure.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"d9a25b0ac94a3598\" href=\"?note=d9a25b0ac94a3598\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-finite.md\">../batch04/58-df-finite.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B,L,\\Phi,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal A},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal A},\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal B},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal B}\\in V\">\\(\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B,L,\\Phi,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal A},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal A},\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal B},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal B}\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Substructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Substructure}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Finite}\">\\(\\mathrm{Finite}\\)</span> are the notions from the cited dependencies.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Reflects}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Reflects}_S:V^8\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflection\\text{-}finite\\text{-}fragment}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Reflects}_S\n(\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B,L,\\Phi,\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal A},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal A},\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal B},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal B})\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Substructure}_S(\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B,L)\n\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(\\Phi)\n\\land\\Phi\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\n(\\mathcal A,L,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal A},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal A})\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\n(\\mathcal B,L,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal B},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal B})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in\\Phi\\;\\forall s\\;\n\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal A,s)\\to\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal B,s)\\land\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal A}(\\varphi,s)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal B}(\\varphi,s)\n\\bigr)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflection\\text{-}finite\\text{-}fragment}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Reflects}_S\n(\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B,L,\\Phi,\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal A},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal A},\n\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal B},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal B})\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Substructure}_S(\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B,L)\n\\land\\mathrm{Finite}(\\Phi)\n\\land\\Phi\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\n(\\mathcal A,L,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal A},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal A})\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\n(\\mathcal B,L,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal B},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal B})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in\\Phi\\;\\forall s\\;\n\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal A,s)\\to\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal B,s)\\land\\bigl(\n\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal A}(\\varphi,s)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal B}(\\varphi,s)\n\\bigr)\\bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the set-coded finite-fragment elementarity relation needed by reflection arguments.</li>\n<li>The full Lévy reflection principle is a metatheorem asserting, for each fixed finite formula set, arbitrarily large ranks with this agreement relative to the ambient universe. The ambient universe is a proper class, so it must not be inserted as an argument of the set-valued satisfaction predicate.</li>\n<li>The earlier statement quantified over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> as though it were a set-coded structure and left the language, assignments, and two satisfaction relations implicit.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"ta